🪨 Rock vs Mine Prediction
📘 Project Overview

This project predicts whether a sonar signal bounced off a metal cylinder (Mine) or a rock on the sea floor.
It uses machine learning classification techniques to analyze the features of sonar signals and determine the correct category.

🎯 Objective

To build and evaluate a model that can accurately classify sonar signals as Rock (R) or Mine (M) based on numerical frequency data.

📊 Dataset

Dataset Name: Sonar Mines vs Rocks Dataset

Source: UCI Machine Learning Repository

Total Samples: 208

Features: 60 numerical attributes (each representing the energy of a sonar return at different frequencies)

Target:

R → Rock

M → Mine

🧠 Machine Learning Model

Algorithm Used: Logistic Regression (you can mention others if used, like SVM, RandomForest, etc.)

Steps Performed:

Data loading and preprocessing

Splitting dataset into training and test sets (using train_test_split)

Model training

Model evaluation using accuracy score

Prediction for new input data

⚙️ Technologies Used

Python 🐍

NumPy

Pandas

Scikit-learn

